{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LIVE DC HARNESS EVIDENCE for 7c26's two new live cells — they RAN and PASSED.\n\nRUN: GitHub Actions run 30682512839 (workflow external-integration.yml, --ref main, dispatched\nafter 7c26 merged as 08b47eb78e).\nJOB: \"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)\" — job id 91322195258 — SUCCESS.\nRESULT LINE: `[jira-live-canary] collected=19 executed=19 skipped=0` / `19 passed in 16.73s`.\n\nTHE TWO CELLS THIS TICKET ADDED, both in tests/external/live_jira_dc/:\n  * test_an_issue_resolves_by_its_immutable_numeric_id — PASSED\n  * test_a_deleted_issue_fails_by_key_AND_by_id_so_deletions_are_not_masked — PASSED\n\nWHY THAT COUNT IS THE PROOF rather than the bare \"success\". The previous fully-green DC harness\nrun (30662366152) reported collected=17 executed=17 skipped=0. This run reports 19/19 with\nskipped=0. So the delta is exactly this ticket's two cells, and — because skipped=0 — neither was\nsilently skipped, which is the failure mode that matters for live cells (a missing harness makes\nthem skip rather than fail, and a skipped live cell is not evidence of anything). Both executed\nagainst a real, ephemeral Jira Data Center instance and both passed.\n\nONE JOB IN THE SAME RUN FAILED AND IT IS NOT OURS. \"external integration (live services)\"\n(job 91322195282) failed in tests/external/test_execution_mode_live.py — the live LLM workflow\ntests (`assert res[\"status\"] == \"succeeded\"` on a `live_single_turn` workflow run, and\n`verdict[\"coverage\"].get(\"llm_ran\") is True`). That is the LLM execution-mode suite, not the Jira\nDC harness; it touches no adapter, transport, or binding code. Recorded explicitly so the run's\noverall red does not later get misread as a DC failure — counts are not causes, and neither is a\nrun-level conclusion.\n\nWHAT REMAINS UNSETTLED, unchanged and already documented on this ticket: a real project MOVE is\nnot performable through pycontribs/jira 3.10.5 (verified at RUNTIME — there is no move member;\n`move_to_backlog` is Agile and `move_version` is versions), and DC's move is a UI wizard. So what\n`GET /issue/{oldKey}` returns after a genuine move stays OPEN. The live cells above cover what IS\ncheckable on this harness — resolution by the immutable numeric id, and that a deleted issue fails\nby key AND by id so a deletion cannot masquerade as a re-key. The remediation (key on the numeric\nid, re-ask by id on a 404) does not depend on which of 200/301/404 a moved key returns, which is\nwhy it was safe to land ahead of that answer."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785557601188845001,"uuid":"a14476b1-9958-4e9a-9cef-b70fc28e186a"}